# Phase 2 Walkthrough: MediaPipe & Computer Vision Foundation

## Summary of Changes
In **Phase 2**, we integrated **MediaPipe Hands** into the Python FastAPI microservice to detect hands, extract the 21 hand landmarks, and generate normalized 63-dimensional feature vectors for downstream machine learning gesture classification.

---

## 1. Key Components Created / Modified

- **[mediapipe_engine.py](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/ai-service/app/ml/mediapipe_engine.py)**:
  - `MediaPipeHandDetector` class with image decoding (`decode_base64_image`).
  - Landmark extraction with `mp.solutions.hands.Hands`.
  - Normalization pipeline (`normalize_landmarks`) providing translation invariance (shifted relative to wrist) and scale invariance (divided by max dimension).
  - Flattened 63-element feature vector generator.
- **[predict_schema.py](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/ai-service/app/schemas/predict_schema.py)**:
  - `PredictRequest`: Validates base64 string.
  - `PredictResponse`: Returns `hand_detected`, `handedness`, `landmarks_count`, `landmarks`, `normalized_landmarks`, `feature_vector`, `feature_vector_size`, and status `message`.
- **[main.py](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/ai-service/app/main.py)**:
  - Updated `POST /predict` endpoint to execute the full decoding and detection pipeline.
- **[test_detector.py](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/ai-service/test_detector.py)**:
  - Standalone verification script supporting both automated offline testing with sample images and live interactive webcam verification (`--webcam`).
- **[sample_hand.jpg](file:///d:/college/Projects/ISL_Translator/ai-service/tests/sample_hand.jpg)**:
  - Bundled sample hand image for deterministic local testing.

